INT. DRIFTING SALT-HARVEST BARGE - AIRLOCK - CONTINUOUS

Red emergency light. Frost on the walls. Pressure alarm pulsing.

NADIR SOLOMON (40s, pilot) slams the inner hatch. SOLENNE ARQUETTE (20s, engineer) jams a wrench into the wheel. BAXTER "BAX" ULLMAN (50s, quartermaster) hauls a crate against the door.

NADIR
It's through the hull--

SOLENNE
Not through, it's--

BAX
Everybody off the wall!

SOLENNE
I need ten seconds--

NADIR
We don't have ten!

BAX
Then make it five!

The hatch BANGS from outside. All three leap back, then lunge at the wheel together.

SOLENNE
Hold it!

NADIR
Holding!

BAX
Don't hold it, turn it!

SOLENNE
Turn it left! Left!

The wheel locks. The alarm cuts out. They slide down the wall, breathing hard.

NADIR
(quiet)
Whatever that was, it knows we're in here.
